From 00a4c493a65798f6bb05140935f0c62cf27e7290 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zingzy <zingzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:29:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] gpui: record each frame's elements and text for driver
 tools

Tools that drive an app from outside it need to know what is on screen:
where each element is, what it responds to, where it was built and what
text it shows. The accessibility tree only holds elements with an id and
an explicit role. This records every element and painted line while a
window flag is on, and keeps cached views in the record.
